          %p
            Given an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coring"} coring
            or even a more general additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/grouplike+element"} grouplike element
            there are several related (but in general nonequivalent) notions of connections.
          %p
            As explained in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/grouplike+element"} grouplike element
            = succeed "-coring" do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with a grouplike element one associates a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-free+differential+graded+algebra"} semi-free differential graded algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega A = \Omega(A,C)
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+for+a+differential+graded+algebra"} connection
            for the corresponding Amitsur complex.
          %p
            Let now
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\Delta,\epsilon)
            be an
            = succeed "-coring" do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            and
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Omega A,d)
            its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amitsur+complex"} Amitsur complex
          %p
            A
            %strong connection
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla:M\otimes_A\Omega^\bullet\to M\otimes_A\Omega^{\bullet+1}
            on a module
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
            (in the sense of the entry
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+for+a+differential+graded+algebra"} connection for a differential graded algebra
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_M|_M
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\cong M\otimes_A A
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi M
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho^M:M\to M\otimes_A C
            is a right
            = succeed "-" do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coaction"} coaction
            then the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi M
                  %mo :
                  %mi m
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi m
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla|_M:m\mapsto \rho^M(m)-m\otimes g
          %p
            determines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat connection
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-coaction" do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi m
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi g
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho^M(m)=\nabla(m)+m\otimes g.
          %p
            This amounts to a
            %em
              bijection between
              = succeed "-coactions" do
                %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystalline+cohomology"} crystalline cohomology
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+connection"} Grothendieck connection
          %h2#connections_on_comodules_directly Connections on comodules directly
          %p
            One the other hand, one can consider more generally additive comonads, and define connections on comodules over them rather directly. Or dually one can work with connection on modules over
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+monad"} additive monad
          %p
            Menini and Ştefan first define an intermediate notion of a quasi-connection for monads. Let
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\mu,\eta)
            an additive monad in
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo :
                  %mi TM
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu:TM\to M
            an action on some object
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %strong quasi-connection
            on
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a map
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi TM
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla:M\to TM
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi ν
                  %mo −
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi TM
                  %mo −
                  %mi η
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi ν
                  %mo :
                  %mi TM
                  %mo →
                  %mi TM
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nabla \circ \nu - \mu\circ T(\nabla) = id_{TM} -  \eta\circ\nu: TM\to TM.
          %p
            A quasi-connection is a
            %strong connection
            if, in addition,
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nu\circ\nabla = 0.
          %p
            For every connection in Menini–Ştefan sense, one defines its
            %strong curvature
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\nabla : M\to T^2 M
            by the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a2a5cf2350827d08c7540acd3ae5895dd2768316_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mn 2
                      %mi M
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi TM
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F_\nabla := (id_{T^2 M} - \eta_{TM}\circ\mu_M)\circ T(\nabla)\circ\nabla.
          %p
            As usually, we define a
            %strong flat connection
            as a connection whose curvature vanishes.
          %p In this setting one again has a bijection between flat connections and descent data.
